# Story: an editor is in front. ⌃⌥Space goes down to look around, and ⌃⌥↓ follows at once, rolled off the fingers. Of the nine keys that ship ⌃⌥↓ is bound to
# nothing, and Arbor used to ask for it only once the tap had become a hold, 0.3 s later: until then it went to the editor, which
# does with it whatever it does. The arrows are the peek's for as long as its key is down, from the press on (F51, acceptance 4; board 1.80).
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
zoom 102
# The control: with no peek on such a key is the app's. (`app-got` names the last key the app in front got.)
key ctrl+opt+up
expect app-got ctrl+opt+up
keydown ctrl+opt+space
wait 0.1
key ctrl+opt+down
expect app-got ctrl+opt+up
keyup ctrl+opt+space
expect camera 103
# Decided, and the key still down: nothing happens, and nothing goes astray.
keydown ctrl+opt+space
wait 0.5
key ctrl+opt+escape
expect camera 103
key ctrl+opt+down
expect app-got ctrl+opt+up
expect camera 103
keyup ctrl+opt+space
# A tap gives them back at its release.
key ctrl+opt+space
key ctrl+opt+down
expect app-got ctrl+opt+down
# Unless the person said so themselves: an app that keeps its own ⌃⌥ comes to the front with the key still down.
pass-through com.example.notes on
expect ok
focus 102
keydown ctrl+opt+space
wait 0.5
focus 103
key ctrl+opt+up
expect app-got ctrl+opt+up
keyup ctrl+opt+space
